file_path: skills/style-guide/SKILL.md
content:
---
name: style-guide
description: Use when writing or reviewing code in this project to apply the team's code style conventions (2-space indentation, named exports only, named function declarations for module-level functions).
---

# Style Guide

Apply these conventions to all code you write or review in this project.

## 1. Indentation: 2 spaces

Indent with 2 spaces. Never use tabs or 4-space indentation.

```ts
// Correct
export function total(items: number[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0);
}

// Incorrect (4 spaces)
export function total(items: number[]): number {
    return items.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 0);
}
```

## 2. Named exports only

Do not use default exports. Export every public binding by name.

```ts
// Correct
export function parseConfig(raw: string): Config {
  return JSON.parse(raw);
}

// Incorrect
export default function parseConfig(raw: string): Config {
  return JSON.parse(raw);
}
```

When importing, use the named form: `import { parseConfig } from './config';`.

## 3. Module-level functions: named function declarations

Declare top-level functions with `function name() {}`. Arrow functions are fine for inline callbacks.

```ts
// Correct: module-level function
export function formatName(first: string, last: string): string {
  return `${first} ${last}`;
}

// Incorrect: module-level arrow function
export const formatName = (first: string, last: string): string => {
  return `${first} ${last}`;
};

// Correct: arrow function as an inline callback
const doubled = values.map((v) => v * 2);
```

